lines=['# CP formation-time CE: fixed-case preview only','', 'Status: complete score/rank sealing, full label evaluation NOT started. The full score job was already running when the parent narrowed the next step; it completed once without reading labels. Only the prespecified 18 same-day added/removed examples have subsequently been joined to existing labels, after their membership was sealed. No formula or ordering changes.', '', '## Formula and units','', 'r_j = log(C_j/C_previous same-source observation). Original s_j = max(1.4826 * median(abs(r) over 63 observations strictly before j), 1e-8); z_j=max(s_j,log(1.001)). Native scale is z frozen at the true formation anchor, not the current rolling s/z.', '', 'Original amount B_j = median(amount over 21 observations strictly before j); u_j=tanh(r_j/s_j); b_j=tanh(log(amount_j/B_j)); m_j=1+0.5*abs(u_j)*b_j. This b is the original cache v, renamed only in this explanation to avoid collision with new volatility-budget v. m is dimensionless, with range (0.5,1.5); it is reused verbatim, not recomputed.', '', 'D_t=original cp.displacement=sum(new upward price-frontier log increments since the true anchor); K_t=original cp.credit=sum(m_j*new upward log frontier increment). Both D and K have log-return units. They are related evidence, not independent tests. Original certification requires both >=sqrt(5)*frozen z and a new frontier increment.', '', 'v_j^2=max(mean(last 21 valid same-source r strictly before j squared),log(1.001)^2). It needs all 21 prior valid observations; otherwise UNKNOWN. The current signal r_j does not enter v_j, but it does enter later forecasts. Same-source r history continues across E0/CP resets and receipts, while source change clears this history.', '', 'V_t=sum(v_j^2 over original observations after the true CP anchor through t); n is that same exact observation count. Original start/E0_down_reset/lower_anchor reset V/n at their anchor day, which contributes zero. E0_invalid/unprepared/source change clear V/n. Ordinary pullbacks keep accumulating both. On receipt_consumed, compute CE=min(D,K)/sqrt(V) FIRST, then reset V/n with the receipt close as the next anchor.', '', 'sqrt(V) is a formation-period cumulative second-moment amplitude. No serial-independence or zero-mean claim has been established; it is not an exact variance of a sum, p-value, win probability, or forecast Sharpe. CE has no gate, n cap, delay, account state change, or revived old certificate.', '', '## Mechanism and cautions','', 'CE can demote evidence accumulated slowly or after high recent volatility, but can also strongly favor a new one-day jump following a quiet period. It is not inherently anti-chasing. The 8 cases are already selected historical examples and cannot establish or refute aggregate validity.', '', '600056 on 2022-03-03 and 03-30 has n=1 in both. CE changes 3.866596 to 1.142547 because the prior21 RMS changes 0.024630 to 0.083463 despite nearly equal current displacement. These cases show a volatility-scale issue, not a long-duration accumulation explanation.', '', 'All 103766 legal candidate rows have finite CE; original PVR-unknown 91 slots remain fixed. All 4040575 source observations have exact native credit/displacement/anchor/frozen-scale lineage checks; 4893 entire-prefix comparisons pass. Original baseline 27990 selected rows matches exactly. 15530 i_buy=false candidate rows remain, with no acceptance filter. No original indicator or account run.', '', '## Fixed eight cases', '', c[['sid','day','CE','formation_n','variance_budget','source_displacement','source_credit','sigma_frozen','sigma_recent','source_m','original_CP_excess','original_PVR','original_rank','CE_rank','K','membership']].to_string(index=False), '', '## Daily budget contributions', '', con.to_string(index=False), '', '## Same-day membership counts', '', pd.read_csv(O/'FIXED_DATES_PVR_COUNTS.csv').to_string(index=False), '', 'Four dates have N<=K: 2022-03-04/03-22/03-24 and 2024-07-29. Their selected members are identical despite changed ranks. 300182 2022-01-04 is outside both top20 (42 ->112), so its CE change does not affect membership.', '', '## Predetermined positive and negative examples', '', 'Each of 2022-01-04/03-03/03-30: first three added by sealed CE order, and first three removed by original order. Chosen without labels, then all 18 displayed. Returns and MAEs are the original native-price 5/20-observation paths, not realized trade outcomes or account returns.', '', p[['day','membership','sid','original_rank','CE_rank','formation_n','source_r','sigma_recent','original_CP_excess','CE','ret5','ret20','mae5','mae20']].to_string(index=False), '', '## Direct single-day-jump tilt check', '', summ.to_string(index=False), '', '## Limits', '', 'Current-survivor/static future-selected stock universe and non-PIT industry/market-cap sources remain. This is consumed development history, not out-of-sample. The entire pool evaluation remains paused. 2026 right censoring and missing labels must stay UNKNOWN. Daily next-open labels are not verified executable fills. Original root epoch literal None must be preserved with keep_default_na=False; root-identity sensitivity remains. No parameter sweep, new portfolio, threshold optimization, or strategy promotion.']
